---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import ActionMatcher from "../components/ui/ActionMatcher.astro";
import Button from "../components/ui/Button.astro";
import Callout from "../components/ui/Callout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/ui/Hero.astro";
import PillarCard from "../components/ui/PillarCard.astro";
import Section from "../components/ui/Section.astro";
import Signature from "../components/ui/Signature.astro";
import Stat from "../components/ui/Stat.astro";
import Stitch from "../components/ui/Stitch.astro";
---

<Page
	title="Automate Ethically"
	description="A movement for automation with a human in the loop: laws that keep a person accountable for every automated decision, software built on that principle, and help retraining for durable work."
>
	<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify({
		"@context": "https://schema.org",
		"@type": "Organization",
		name: "Automate Ethically",
		url: "https://automate-ethically.com",
		logo: "https://automate-ethically.com/favicon.svg",
		sameAs: ["https://jdetle.com", "https://github.com/jdetle/automate-ethically"],
	})} />

	<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 1: hero headline + subhead -->
	<!-- The site's one ink-shift headline and its one weave ground live here. -->
	<Hero
		eyebrow="A civic demand"
		title="A human should make the decision."
		size="display"
		inkShift
		weave
		chips
		titleId="hero-title"
	>
		<p class="ae-hero-sub">
			Cameras watch your street. Machines answer your insurance claim. Data
			centers rise at the edge of town. None of them can be held accountable.
			A person can.
		</p>
		<p class="ae-hero-urgent">
			The laws are being written right now. Forty-five states are debating
			them this session. The rulebook gets set with you, or without you.
		</p>
		<div class="ae-cta-row">
			<Button href="/act">What you can do this week</Button>
			<Button href="#manifesto" variant="secondary">Read the argument</Button>
		</div>
	</Hero>

	<Stitch />

	<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 2: manifesto -->
	<Section
		id="manifesto"
		eyebrow="Why now"
		title="The anger is real. Aim it at the rulebook."
		titleId="manifesto-title"
	>
		<div class="ae-prose">
			<p>
				You are right to be angry. The cameras went up without asking you. The
				data center got its permits before you heard about it. The machine
				denied the claim, and no one's name was on the denial.
			</p>
			<p>
				But a data center is a totem. Block one, and the machines it served
				move one county over. The win that lasts is a law: wherever an
				automated system touches your life, a person decides, and that person
				answers for it.
			</p>
			<p>
				Machines cannot take responsibility. Companies will not volunteer it.
				Rules change when neighbors organize, city by city, then state by
				state. That is how it has always worked.
			</p>
		</div>
		<figure class="ae-epigraph">
			<blockquote>
				The loom did not remove the weaver. A person still chose the pattern,
				punched the cards, examined the cloth, and signed the bolt.
			</blockquote>
			<figcaption>The rule we intend to keep, drawn from the Jacquard loom of 1804.</figcaption>
		</figure>
	</Section>

	<Stitch />

	<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 11: urgency stats framing (numbers + citations stay; see FACTS.md) -->
	<Section id="clock" eyebrow="Evidence, cited" title="The clock is the rulebook" titleId="clock-title" wide>
		<p class="ae-plain">
			None of this is hypothetical. It is already on your street, your power
			bill, and your legislature's calendar.
		</p>
		<div class="ae-stats">
			<Stat
				value="6,000"
				accent="cobalt"
				label="communities watched by one company's license-plate cameras, across 49 states"
				source={{
					href: "https://www.ipm.org/news/2026-08-17/flock-safety-tightens-safeguards-as-states-cities-question-surveillance-network",
					label: "Stateline, Aug 2026",
				}}
			/>
			<Stat
				value="426&thinsp;TWh"
				accent="coral"
				label="projected US data-center electricity by 2030, more than double 2024, and nearly half of all US demand growth"
				source={{
					href: "https://www.iea.org/reports/energy-and-ai/energy-demand-from-ai",
					label: "IEA, Energy and AI",
				}}
			/>
			<Stat
				value="1,561"
				accent="ink"
				label="AI bills introduced in 45 states this session. The rules get written with you, or without you."
				source={{
					href: "https://www.multistate.ai/artificial-intelligence-ai-legislation",
					label: "multistate.ai, Mar 2026",
				}}
			/>
		</div>
		<Callout tone="sun" layout="banner" title="This is winnable." class="ae-winnable">
			<p>
				More than 50 communities have already
				paused or canceled camera contracts since January
				(<a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/02/17/nx-s1-5612825/flock-contracts-canceled-immigration-survillance-concerns">NPR</a>),
				and Montana already requires a human to review AI-driven agency
				decisions. Despair does not produce turnout. A specific, winnable ask
				does.
			</p>
			<p>
				Facts checked Aug 2026. Sources and our correction policy live in the
				open at <a href="/facts">FACTS.md</a>. See
				<a href="/states">what's already real, state by state</a>.
			</p>
		</Callout>
	</Section>

	<Stitch />

	<Section
		id="pillars"
		eyebrow="Three ways in, three different kinds of commitment"
		title="Three pillars, one principle"
		titleId="pillars-title"
		tint
		wide
	>
		<div class="ae-pillars">
			<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 3: pillar Organize -->
			<PillarCard
				id="organize"
				kicker="Pillar 01 · A demand"
				title="Organize"
				tone="cobalt"
				href="/pillars/organize"
				linkLabel="The ordinance &amp; the script"
			>
				<p>
					One ordinance, one clause: automated decisions by your city require a
					named human reviewer. Bring it to a council meeting. We wrote the
					script.
				</p>
			</PillarCard>
			<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 4: pillar Build ethically -->
			<PillarCard
				id="build"
				kicker="Pillar 02 · A practice"
				title="Build ethically"
				href="/about#projects"
				linkLabel="See what we're building"
			>
				<pre class="ae-musts">MUST  a named person approves each release
MUST  every automated decision is appealable
MUST  the human can always say no</pre>
				<Signature name="signed: a person, every time" />
			</PillarCard>
			<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 5: pillar Retrain -->
			<PillarCard
				id="retrain"
				kicker="Pillar 03 · Solidarity"
				title="Retrain"
				tone="coral"
				href="/toolkit/retrain"
				linkLabel="Start while you're still employed"
			>
				<p>
					Your job is on a list somewhere. That is not your failure. Learn the
					next field while you still have this one, alongside people doing the
					same.
				</p>
			</PillarCard>
		</div>
	</Section>

	<Stitch />

	<Section id="get-involved" wide>
		<ActionMatcher name="home" id="matcher" heading="What can you do?" />
	</Section>

	<Section eyebrow="The movement" title="Neighbors, builders, and organizers." titleId="about-pointer-title">
		<p class="ae-plain">
			We intend to form a registered political committee. Until that exists, we
			are not asking for money.
		</p>
		<p class="ae-aside">
			<a href="/about">Who's behind this, and the software we're building
			alongside it &rarr;</a>
		</p>
	</Section>

	<div class="ae-coda">
		<p>
			&ldquo;Physics was the easy part. Everyone still has to become different
			at the same time, and everyone has a reason to go last.&rdquo;
		</p>
	</div>
</Page>

<style>
	/*
	 * :global because this class is handed to <Callout> as a prop, so it
	 * lands on an element Astro scopes to that component rather than to this
	 * page. Without it the selector never matched anything and the banner sat
	 * flush against the stats above it with no gap at all.
	 */
	:global(.ae-winnable) {
		margin: 32px 0 4px;
	}

	/* The three MUSTs are a contract, so they are set as one — monospaced,
	   unwrapped, and never reflowed into prose. */
	.ae-musts {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
		font-family: var(--ae-mono);
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
		color: var(--ae-muted);
		white-space: pre-wrap;
	}
</style>
